<title>USA: ArQule shares rise after market debut. [CORRECTED 19:51 GMT]</title>
<headline>ArQule shares rise after market debut. [CORRECTED 19:51 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of ArQule Inc rose on Wednesday after the company's initial public offering.</p>
<p>The stock rose 1-11/16 to 13-11/16.</p>
<p>It offered 2.5 million shares, up from its previous estimate of two million shares, which priced at $12 each, in the middle of its estimated pricing range of $11 to $13.</p>
<p>(Corrects number of shares offered from 2 million).</p>
<p>Hambrecht &amp; Quist was the lead underwriter of the offering. ArQule develops and identifies chemical compounds which it sells to the pharmaceutical and biotechnology industries.</p>
